,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-04T11:04:02Z","updated_at":"2025-11-04T11:04:02Z","body":"So how is it better than #94171?\r\nYou can set ScrollContainer's max size, make scrollbars invisible, and you will get effectively the same thing.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3485354749/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3485962556","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3485962556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3485962556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Px5E8","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-04T13:16:18Z","updated_at":"2025-11-04T13:16:28Z","body":"> So how is it better than https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94171?\r\nYou can set ScrollContainer's max size, make scrollbars invisible, and you will get effectively the same thing.\r\n\r\nBecause that is giving ScrollContainer the responsibility of limiting size, and necessitates a workaround - making invisible scrollbars - to achieve the same effect. \r\nJust like every other subtype of Container does one thing, ScrollContainer should do its one thing, namely scrolling, and this SizeContainer would do its one thing, namely limiting size. \r\n\r\n> Can this new node enable the ScrollContainer to start scrolling when its size reaches max, otherwise, the ScrollContainer expands normally in size?\r\n\r\nIt should. If it doesn't, then there's an implementation issue. WIll try it, and fix if it doesn't work. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3485962556/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3487457069","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3487457069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3487457069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7P3l8t","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-04T18:20:15Z","updated_at":"2025-11-04T19:49:27Z","body":"Added support for ScrollContainer. This required a bit more of an involved change since there was no existing way to get the \"maximum size\" a Control *could* fill. I put it as the `get_combined_minimum_size()` by default and then provided a specific override for ScrollContainer. I don't think any of the other Control types need/support something like that but I might be wrong. \r\n\r\nEdit: maybe this could be used for autowrap with Labels, will investigate","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3487457069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3491628683","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3491628683","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3491628683,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QHgaL","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T14:46:28Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T14:46:28Z","body":"@KoBeWi I saw your comment on the proposal, https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13534#issuecomment-3490999703. Discussing here since it is implementation-level, not feature discussion.\r\n\r\nCould you please give more details on what you are suggesting for the implementation, so that we can discuss it, and I can maybe work towards migrating the implementation to it? \r\n\r\nThe current `get_combined_maximum_size()` approach is quite nice, in my opinion, since it doesn't touch any existing code, meaning 0 risk of compatibility breakage, but I am completely open to anything that would be better than it. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3491628683/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3491733644","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3491733644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3491733644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QH6CM","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T15:03:31Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T15:03:31Z","body":"It would be like https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94171 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13568, except instead of an exposed property in the relevant node, the max size would be set by SizeContainer.\r\n\r\nThat means Control would get `custom_maximum_size` that can be used internally by derived nodes, but the property itself would not be available to the user. It's a weird design, but it would allow SizeContainer to be more functional.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3491733644/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3491779960","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3491779960","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3491779960,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QIFV4","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T15:10:22Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T15:10:22Z","body":"How would that be any better than the `get_combined_maximum_size()` approach the PR currently employs?\r\n\r\nSidenote: The way #94171 was implemented wouldn't have worked for what this PR is trying to accomplish. It would only be a limit on the `largest_child_min_size` which isn't the expand-until-maximum-size-reached design this PR adds (and what people seem to be wanting). ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://a