ntbh I missed when you changed it. That approach makes sense.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3492026644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3492039547","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3492039547","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3492039547,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QJEt7","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T15:59:07Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T16:02:50Z","body":"That's weird, I have that exact same setup (well a VBox instead of HBox) and it works with the latest version of the PR. Does your size container have a `maximum_size` set?\r\n\r\nEdit: It shouldn't matter, I checked the code (I don't have access to my machine which has the binary at the moment), and `maximum_size` only acts as an upper bound if defined, if not defined it will just expand to infinity. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3492039547/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3492146437","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3492146437","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3492146437,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QJe0F","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T16:23:38Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T16:23:38Z","body":"I'm using the latest version and I do have maximum size set. Can you share your scene?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3492146437/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3492560967","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3492560967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3492560967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QLEBH","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T17:47:16Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T19:47:45Z","body":"Sure, here's my file https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wign3IAbZnfNcwUqaYeuQMVXofzEbmgo/view?usp=drive_link\r\nThe setup is the same as yours\r\n<img width=\"214\" height=\"197\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4cc0913e-1594-41eb-9595-ad93d09133f8\" />\r\n\r\nEdit: please send yours, so I can compare both on my device and make it work for you scenario - provided it is proper use of the Container","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3492560967/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3494051662","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3494051662","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3494051662,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QQv9O","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T23:30:11Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T23:30:52Z","body":"I found the difference. My ScrollContainer had `vertical_scroll_mode` set to Auto. I noticed your ScrollContainer has `horizontal_scroll_mode` disabled, so I did that (for vertical) and it works. It's weird though, why is orthogonal scroll mode relevant, if the container grows in a different direction?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3494051662/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3494058552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3494058552","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3494058552,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QQxo4","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T23:33:05Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T23:34:07Z","body":"Well, that's definitely unintended behavior. I'll take a look at why it's happening.\r\n\r\nEdit: I had it disabled because getting the horizontal scrollbar was annoying me, which thinking about it, it shouldn't have showed up in the first place :/","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3494058552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3506912455","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3506912455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3506912455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RBzzH","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-08T21:08:53Z","updated_at":"2025-11-08T21:13:12Z","body":"Revamped implementation: \r\n\r\nThis now uses a `custom_maximum_size` property at the `Control` level, which mirrors the `custom_minimum_size` property. The only difference is that it is not visible in the Editor for all `Control` types; `SizeContainer` makes it visible. \r\n`SizeContainer` will also set the value for its children.\r\n\r\nThis now supports `ScrollContainer` properly, as well as reacting to any and all relevant changes in Editor (change size flags, change maximum size, etc).\r\n\r\nI've split it into two commits because the changes in both are significant enough to warrant separate commits. \r\nThe first commit is very noisy because of the depreciation of the minimum size change-related methods and signals being deprecated in favor of new size bounds change versions. Everything is maintained under the `DISABLE_DEPRECATED` definition to avoid breaking compatibility. \r\n* Note: If any other PRs get merged before this one does that call any of the deprecated methods, this PR will need updating, or the Linux disable-everything CI run will fail at compilation time. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3506912455/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3541715130","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3541715130","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3541715130,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TGki6","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T12:59:35Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T12:59:35Z","body":"Ok I gave this another test and compared with the ScrollContainer's max size. You can get the same results with both, so this comment\r\n> It would only be a limit on the largest_child_min_size which isn't the expand-until-maximum-size-reached design this PR adds\r\n\r\nIs not really true. You _can_ do that with the other PR too.\r\n\r\nHowever I noticed a rather crucial difference between the two, which I think makes the other solution better as of now.\r\nScrollContainer's `max_size` is not a real \"maximum size\", but a \"maximum minimum size\". Which means the container will grow its minimum size up to a certain point.\r\nSizeContainer's maximum size is a hard limit. You can't resize it past this threshold. While achieves more or less the same result, it's awkward to use in the editor and may produce \"visual glitches\" when it turns out that more space is available.\r\n<img width=\"396\" height=\"123\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/32702a36-aecf-4172-9492-aa2019930ba7\" />\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3541715130/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3542880068","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3542880068","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3542880068,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TLA9E","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T16:48:03Z","updated_at":"2025-12-03T16:03:53Z","body":"Since both implementations provide the same benefits, which I was mistaken about, and this comes with a much higher implementation cost, I think it would be best to scrap this PR and salvage/re-implement the `ScrollContainer` approach. \r\nIt was a good try - and worth it from a separation of responsibilities aspect - but the cost is starting to outweigh that benefit. \r\n\r\nI won't be able to do so for a few days/until a week from now, so if anyone else is interested in the feature and would like to spearhead it sooner, feel free to. Old PR for reference: #94171 \r\n* Edit Dec 3rd: this might take longer than expected due to activities in my life right now\r\n\r\nAlso, I hope that anyone who has an opinion on the matter and maybe some thoughts about some in-between approach between this and the old PR expresses them here before then. \r\nThis PR will be closed once I (or someone else) open the PR for the `ScrollContainer` approach, as they will definitely collide. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3542880068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3543868433","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3543868433","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3543868433,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TOyQR","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T21:13:27Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T21:13:27Z","body":"Seems like most changes here come from method rename?\r\nThe combination of both approaches would be doing the same as ScrollContainer's `max_size`, but making the property only available via SizeContainer. Which is awkward tbh.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3543868433/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3621312373","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3621312373","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3621312373,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7X2Nd1","user":{"login":"ohboyotero","id":110791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDc5MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero","html_url":"https://github.com/ohboyotero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-06T22:39:06Z","updated_at":"2025-12-06T22:40:45Z","body":"Just throwing in the peanut gallery feedback that hiding size limitation as an unexpected feature on `ScrollContainer` would be very unintuitive and hard to discover for folks. It also feels pretty dirty: to get only a size limit on my container, I add a ScrollContainer (that I'm then going to disable) in order to get the size limitation capability as a side-effect? 🤔 Really?\r\n\r\nI realize that there are technical constraints in separating the two capabilities while also making them work well when combined, so not saying I think it absolutely shouldn't be done. Only emphasizing that I think the dev experience cost is perhaps significantly higher than is being recognized, perhaps to the point of making it worth the pain of a cleaner, but more technically challenging, approach.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3621312373/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638666037","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3638666037","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3638666037,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y4aM1","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T19:37:29Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T19:38:28Z","body":"Initially, I would have agreed that the intuitiveness and discoverability were more important, but as I have worked on this, I realized that the `SizeContainer` solution is wrong because of the need for graceful handling. \r\n\r\nSimply put, a `SizeContainer` would have to do one of the following:\r\n* Have clipping on but no special handling\r\n* Have clipping on and handle it gracefully, to which the best (and only?) solution ends up being a scrollable container, i.e., we're just creating a fancy `ScrollContainer`\r\n\r\nIf we go with the former, we might as well make it a `Container` property. Not only does this greatly simplify the implementation, but it also makes it much more accessible. However, the main drawback is the potentially ugly handling depending on the subtype. But `SizeContainer`'s would be as potentially ugly.\r\n\r\nIf we go with the latter, then we might as well fold it into `ScrollContainer` since having one that has a size limit and one that doesn't would be simply ridiculous. This would have the discoverability and intuitiveness issues but a guaranteed pretty handling. \r\n\r\nIn both cases, `SizeContainer` becomes the worse solution of the two options. \r\nPersonally, I actually believe the former (namely `Container`-level handling) is better. Yes, it may not be pretty if the sub-type doesn't handle it gracefully, but it's an advanced feature; it doesn't have to work in every scenario magically. \r\n\r\n*Note: Implementation-wise, both of these are fairly trivial to implement. This PR's implementation is messy because of the property being at the `Container` level for proper child handling but set by `SizeContainer`, which would disappear no matter which path we go with. They would both represent similar development and maintaining workloads, significantly lower than this PR's so we don't need to worry about that.*","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638666037/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643208200","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3643208200","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3643208200,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZJvII","user":{"login":"ohboyotero","id":110791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDc5MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero","html_url":"https://github.com/ohboyotero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohboyotero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T18:19:02Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T18:20:37Z","body":"> Personally, I actually believe the former (namely `Container`-level handling) is better.\r\n\r\nAgreed. I understand the \"one container type, one function\" ideology, but there are a few things that just make so much sense to push to the root imho as they are so often required together.  This (min_size, max_size, \"overflow mode\") feels like one of them. Personally, I also find myself adding inner/outer `MarginContainer`s _everywhere_.\r\n\r\nSimilar sentiment from @shadowblitz16 here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8333#issuecomment-3523359431\r\n\r\n> we're just creating a fancy ScrollContainer\r\n\r\nYeah, that makes sense. If the max_size functionality does end up having to be merged into ScrollContainer, it would be great to rename ScrollContainer accordingly to reflect the greater functionality (e.g., `OverflowContainer` or `ConstrainedContainer` or something), but I imagine that is far too big/breaking a change.\r\n\r\nI hate this suggestion tbh, but maybe just add a type alias with the new name? That way the larger functionality is at least discoverable in scanning through the docs/types, and the core intent behind use of the component can be clarified by selecting the more appropriate name for code readability?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643208200/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3941899177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112364#issuecomment-3941899177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112364","id":3941899177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q9Jup","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T23:19:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T23:19:44Z","body":"Closing this PR in favor of #116640, which is a much cleaner implementation and has a lot less baggage than this one. \r\nWill reopen if, for some reason, this solution is favored (the general sentiment from the contributors chat seems to be that the new implementation is the correct path). ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3941899177/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]